# A module of a PTX ISA version that the driver does not support ends the
# run with an error that names the driver's CUDA version, the PTX ISA
# version of the module, and what to do, through both entry points of the
# runtime that load modules (D[release]).
#
# REQUIRES: cuda
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check_ptx_version.py %mdrt_cuda | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: jit: mdrt: the NVIDIA driver supports CUDA
# CHECK: plain: mdrt: the NVIDIA driver supports CUDA
# CHECK: unsupported PTX ISA versions are reported
